                                       "kibana.version":  "9.4.2",
                                       "kibana.alert.rule.parameters":  {
                                                                            "description":  "Detects an encoded PowerShell command whose DECODED payload contains download or\nin-memory execution primitives.\n\nThis rule exists because measurement showed the plain encoded-command rule\n(1131fb39-a497-4a09-b051-4e4c89066f5f) cannot separate benign automation from an\nattack. In the lab\u0027s own alert population, 2 of 4 alerts were benign management\ntooling, and the remaining false positive shared its parent process, image, and\ncommand-line shape with the true positives. Nothing on the command line distinguishes\nthem, because the payload is base64.\n\nThe discriminator is the payload itself, so it is decoded at ingest by\ninfra/elastic/ingest-pipelines/aegis-powershell-decode.json and matched here.\nDecodedCommand is that decoded text, not a Windows event field.\n\nThe two rules are kept together on purpose and carry different severities: the plain\nencoded-command rule is context for hunting, and this one is the alerting rule.\n",
                                                                            "risk_score":  73,
                                                                            "severity":  "high",
